# Contradictory, degenerate and racing inputs.
cuboid 3x3x3

case 4.1 Click a sticker without moving
note No move; feedback says click
wait 0.3
press F@0,0,2
wait 0.3
release
wait 0.3
expect feedback click
expect solved

case 4.2 Drag 5 px (under the 8 px threshold)
note Still a click: no move
drag F@0,0,2 +5,0 0.3
wait 0.3
expect feedback click
expect solved

case 4.3 Exact diagonal drag on F
note Ambiguous: no move, feedback says diagonal
drag F@-2,-2,2 F@2,2,2 0.6
wait 0.3
expect feedback diagonal
expect solved

case 4.4 Drag up, then sideways, in one press
note One press = at most one turn: R, then the sideways part is ignored
press F@2,-2,2
move F@2,2,2 0.4
move F@-2,2,2 0.5
release
settle
expect state R
expect no-feedback turn U
expect no-feedback ignored

case 4.5 Drag from a sticker far off the cube
note Turn R fires as usual; leaving the cube neither orbits nor adds a turn
reset
wait 0.2
drag F@2,-2,2 +0,-260 0.7
settle
expect state R
expect camera-still

case 4.6 Drag from empty space across the cube
note Orbit only: a press that starts off the cube never turns
reset
wait 0.2
drag 80,240 560,240 0.8
settle
expect solved
expect camera-moved
expect no-feedback turn

case 4.7 Right button pressed during a sticker drag
note Second button ignored; the primary drag still turns R
reset
home
wait 0.2
press F@2,-2,2
press +0,0 right
move F@2,2,2 0.4
release
settle
expect feedback ignored: a button is already down
expect state R

case 4.8 Release with no button down
note Ignored
release
wait 0.3
expect feedback ignored: no button was down

case 4.9 Drag a new turn while one animates
note Queued: R then U, in order
reset
wait 0.2
drag F@2,-2,2 F@2,2,2 0.2
drag F@2,0,2 F@-2,0,2 0.1
settle
expect state R 2U

case 4.10 Undo during the animation of the same move
note R finishes, then plays backwards: back to solved
reset
wait 0.2
moves R
wait 0.1
undo
settle
expect solved
expect feedback undo R

case 4.11 Undo with nothing to undo
note Ignored
undo
wait 0.3
expect feedback ignored: nothing to undo

case 4.12 User drag during solver playback
note Remaining solver moves are dropped, the user's turn plays, cube stays unsolved
reset
scramble 20 11
wait 0.3
solve
wait 1.2
drag F@2,-2,2 F@2,2,2 0.3
settle
expect feedback playback interrupted
expect unsolved

case 4.13 Undo during solver playback
note Remaining solver moves are dropped and the last shown move is undone
scramble 20 12
wait 0.3
solve
wait 1.2
undo
settle
expect feedback playback interrupted
expect feedback undo
expect unsolved

case 4.14 Solve pressed twice
note Second press ignored while the first solve runs; one solution plays
solve-latency 0.8
scramble 15 13
wait 0.3
solve
wait 0.2
solve
settle
expect feedback ignored: a solve is already running
expect solved

case 4.15 Move while the solver is thinking
note The late answer is for an old state: dropped; the cube keeps the user's move
scramble 15 14
wait 0.3
solve
wait 0.2
moves R
settle
expect feedback solution dropped
expect unsolved
solve-latency 0

case 4.16 Solve when already solved
note No solve runs
reset
wait 0.2
solve
wait 0.3
expect feedback already solved

case 4.17 Scramble while a sequence is playing
note Jump straight to the scramble; queued turns are discarded
moves R U R U R U
wait 0.2
setup F2 B2
settle
expect state F2 B2

case 4.18 Invalid notation
note Rejected, nothing moves
moves R Q
wait 0.3
expect feedback rejected
expect state F2 B2

case 4.19 Overfill the queue
note Only 64 moves fit in the queue: 64 x R play (= identity), the last 6 are rejected
reset
moves R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R R
expect feedback rejected: too many moves queued
settle
expect solved

case 4.20 Zoom with the wheel during a sticker drag
note The wheel zooms; the drag still produces its turn R
reset
wait 0.2
press F@2,-2,2
move +0,-20 0.1
scroll 2
move F@2,2,2 0.3
release
settle
expect state R
